A||N||21||fropuff||Good glass cleaner???||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||06-22-2000||02:00 PM||||Hey, when I was wet-sanding my Fiero, I got the white crap water (not really crap water) all over the windshield, side windows, and mirrors.  Does anyone know of a really good glass cleaner that would get this stuff off?  It's like a bunch of white spots all over the glass.  There's a lot on there.  When the sun hits it, you can't even see.  It's a hazard.  Thanks.<P>PS: I already tried the MotorTrend brand, Prestone I think it is.  Didn't work worth crap.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Formula||06-22-2000||03:31 PM||||thats just water spots, try windex lol...<P>if you dry it off right after you wash it then it wont do that, it might be on the inside too......you could also try using the gas station stuff||||reg||1
Z||000002||lennyb4||06-22-2000||03:41 PM||||Once you get the spots off, use windex and newspaper. Once your done with that lightly buff the glass with a clean soft terry-cloth hand towel. Man you talk about clean and shiny..WOOOOHOOOO||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||06-22-2000||04:18 PM||||I'm not talking about regular water spots.  These are water spots, but they have the clearcoat and paint in it.  I tried washing if off must have been ten times, but no go.  I also tried with Windex, Stoner glass cleaner, and a nylon brush, and it still won't some off.  I don't know what to do.  Help!!!||||reg||10
Z||000004||olympic||06-22-2000||05:02 PM||||  The only way to get paint off would be to scrape it off with a razor blade or use some sort of solvent like gas or WD-40.  Then wash with strong soap and water to remove any oily residue left by the solvent.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kong||06-22-2000||05:33 PM|||| Try Bon Ami cleanser, It works good for tough crap like that. It comes in a can like comet, but it won't scratch the glass. Another helpful hint from Hot Rod magazine!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Majik||06-22-2000||05:39 PM||||try regular vinager...it does wonders for windows!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  simple fix to hard problem||||reg||1
Z||000007||fropuff||06-22-2000||06:48 PM||||Tried the razor blade on the windshield.  Works the best!!!  I tried vinegar on the sunroof.  It takes it off, but the outline of the spot is still there.  It won't take as long as just with a razor, though!  Oh, does anyone know how I could get this crap off the quarter windows?  Should I try vinegar then the glass cleaner Kong was talking about?  Thanks a lot. ||||reg||10
Z||000008||wilburt||06-22-2000||08:22 PM||||Yes, Kong is right. Bon Ami is an excellent glass cleaner. Only the gold can. It says on the can 'not for windows', but the makers of Rain-X use it to clean windshields. No scratches. I'd use it only on glass sail panels. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||06-22-2000||08:28 PM||||I don't know if I'm a complete retard, but are my sail panels glass or plastic?  I have an 86 GT.  Thanks.||||reg||10
Z||000010||wilburt||06-22-2000||08:47 PM||||I believe all stock GT are glass. Notchbacks are plastic. I could be wrong, someone here knows for sure.<P>BTW Bon Ami is good for glass, but sure can't clean a sink like A-Jax!||||reg||1
Z||000011||wilburt||06-22-2000||09:13 PM||||I just walked outside, and on my '87 GT the sail panels are not glass. Looks like glass, kinda has checks like glass. I think Lexan? I don't know, but it ain't glass. <P>I'm sorry, and hope I didn't cause harm.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fropuff||06-22-2000||09:21 PM||||Does anyone have a spare quarter window on hand?  The glass cleaner I was told about scratched the glass and started to melt around the edges.  Looks worse than before.  Give me a price.  ||||reg||1
