Z||000014||fropuff||06-22-2000||09:25 PM||||HA!  I was just kidding, Wilbert.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Oreif||06-23-2000||01:51 AM||||To clean your glass use Rain-X Glass polish. I used this to remove the fine scratches left from a bad dew wipe. Works great! If it removes scratches it'll remove paint.<P>Couldn't delete the second one.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Oreif||06-23-2000||01:51 AM||||To clean your glass use Rain-X Glass polish. I used this to remove the fine scratches left from a bad dew wipe. Works great! If it removes scratches it'll remove paint.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Standard||06-23-2000||04:47 AM||||The Fastback GT quarter windows are a type of Acrylic.  What kind I'm not sure, but be careful what you use to clean them.  Make sure anything you use is safe to use on them.<P>Go here.. <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/fierov6/OSG/rear-quarter-windows.html#clean" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/_XMCM/fierov6/OSG/rear-quarter-windows.html#clean</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Oreif||06-23-2000||10:16 AM||||I've never tried it on GT sailpanels but Meguires makes a plastic polish I have used on my tail lens' and the clear plastic over the dash. This may work to clean your sail panels.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||06-23-2000||10:44 AM||||'84s had glass sail panels (I gotta have some <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  The rest of the notchbacks had plastic/Lexan/plexiglass.||||reg||1
Z||000020||bHooper||06-23-2000||11:11 AM||||a real fine grade of steal wool works great on <B>glass</B>.  i used to use this on my '66 mustang convertible all the time... great for chrom, also.<P>lighter fluid is also usefull for removing things from glass.<P>you might want to try both on the windshield... as for the quarter windows, they are a lexan/plastic material.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000021||fropuff||06-26-2000||06:04 PM||||Worked great!  I use the vinegar, wipe off, WD-40 & razor, wash off, Rain-X, wipe off.  Does it look good!  I did that on my sunroof but not on the windshield.  I just used WD-40 and a razor on that.  Turned out, but there's still some outlines of the spots.  Doesn't matter anyway, I just found a crack on the bottom right corner.  Used to be a crack, but the FROST (yes, frost) last week cracked it.  Oh, well.  When I get insurance, I'll get the windshield replacement.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks for all the replys.  They've been a lot of help!||||reg||1
